   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Steam\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem**  \n",
    "Recommender systems that rely mainly on shared tags or genres can suggest games a user is unlikely to enjoy, because they ignore how the user actually plays.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question**  \n",
    "Does combining user behaviour features with game features predict a user’s enjoyment of an unseen game more accurately than tag overlap alone?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Features**\n",
    "- User behaviour: genre mix, log-scaled playtime, recency of play, preference for older or newer titles\n",
    "- Game: genre, tags, release age, review sentiment, price\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task**  \n",
    "Binary classification of whether a user recommends a game.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Evaluation**  \n",
    "AUC, F1 and Precision@10, using a time-based train/validation/test split.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hypotheses**\n",
    "- **H1:** Multi-feature models outperform a tag-overlap baseline.\n",
    "- **H2:** Log-scaled playtime is a more reliable engagement signal than raw hours.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Supporting analysis**\n",
    "- Clustering of users (k-means/GMM with PCA) to identify player types\n",
    "- Feature ablation to show which factors matter most"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "17289355",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Anime\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem**  \n",
    "Ratings are often inflated and clustered at the top of the scale, so a single numeric score says little about how much a viewer actually enjoyed a show.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question**  \n",
    "Does the text of user reviews predict a viewer’s enjoyment more accurately than a model using the overall score and metadata alone?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task**  \n",
    "Supervised learning on MyAnimeList-style review data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Comparison**  \n",
    "Text-based models from the module against a score-only baseline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b0d72493",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Game Popularity\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem**  \n",
    "Content creation can inflate or hide a game’s real popularity: some games dominate streaming while few people play them, and others have large player bases but little coverage.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question**  \n",
    "- Can a game’s player-base popularity over time be predicted from content-creation metrics and game attributes?\n",
    "- Does the gap between predicted and actual popularity identify games that are over- or under-represented in content?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Comparison**  \n",
    "Supervised models from the module against a simple baseline."
   ]
  }
